WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.810
<i>Domino Mart</i>

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:12.300
Duelists from the country of the gods?

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:18.600
WRGP contenders Team Ragnarok is the world's 
first professional Riding Duel team.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:22.800
Harald, Dragan and Brave use the three Aesir cards -

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.620
Odin, Thor and Loki. The cards are known as god's messengers.

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:30.270
They're the world's strongest 
cards and have mysterious powers.

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:34.850
They dominated the preliminaries 
with overwhelming power.

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:38.290
Their popularity and skills have made 
them kings of the dueling world.

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:40.280
Kings?  Whatever.

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:42.590
Yusei won't lose to these guys.

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:44.260
Oh, I forgot!

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:47.540
Yusei has D-Wheel practice today!

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:52.660
I won't lose, Jack!

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:55.130
Don't underestimate Wheel of Fortune's power!

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:03.170
They're both doing well.

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:06.580
No matter when the final tournament 
starts, they'll be ready.

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:13.200
The three emperors of Iliaster 
have finally shown themselves.

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:14.790
Look!

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:21.400
Team New World, the team expected to win 
the WRGP, just arrived at the airport!

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:25.330
They're from Iliaster.

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:31.030
Since their inception, Team New World has 
conquered tournaments around the world.

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:34.370
They're one of the top duelist teams.

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:38.190
Their popularity and skills 
are among the world's elite.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:41.500
This article is on every website.

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:45.760
They've changed history 
and are entering the WRGP.

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:49.500
Our goal is to change the future.

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:53.770
We will destroy Neo Domino City.

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:55.860
I won't let them!

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:57.730
We'll protect this city!

00:01:57.730 --> 00:02:00.730
We have to win to save the future!

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:11.590
Will I get there in time?

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:18.370
Move!

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:25.170
Are you okay, Yoshi?

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:27.120
Ouch…

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:28.590
You almost hit me!

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:32.070
I'm sorry!  The D-Wheel controls 
suddenly stopped working!

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:33.610
D-Wheel?

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:41.260
That's a D-Wheel?

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:43.080
I'm very sorry.

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.740
You don't need to apologize, Yoshizo.

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:47.470
It's his fault for jumping into the street.

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:49.660
Jin!

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:51.480
Are you okay?  Are you hurt?

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:52.720
I'm fine.

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:54.900
Ouch...

00:02:57.270 --> 00:02:59.660
It's swollen.  You have to ice it.

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:01.260
I'm fine.  This is nothing.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:05.120
Take it easy.  Our hotel is nearby.

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:12.240
Riding Duels.

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:15.380
These duels evolved in the world of speed.

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:22.220
The people with the legendary marks who 
risked their lives were known as 5D's.

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:43.500
Reach out your hand and 
grab a bright tomorrow

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:53.610
Soar in the infinite skies  BELIEVE IN NEXUS

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:59.850
No one can stop my wild impulses

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:05.820
My hand sweats as the battle 
intensifies  This Heart Beat

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:11.600
I can't avoid this fearsome battle

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:17.200
I don't want it to end here  Go For It!!

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:23.570
Stand up  Don't tremble in fear alone

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:29.380
Remember that you have 
friends waiting for you

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:35.690
I'm not scared and I'll never give 
up, no matter how powerful the enemy

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:41.990
With real courage, I'll never lose

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:11.720
New Rivals

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:26.140
All good.

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:27.370
Thank you.

00:05:27.570 --> 00:05:30.380
I'm surprised you can stay 
in a place like this.

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:32.380
We only use this place to sleep.

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:36.110
We came from the outskirts to enter the WRGP.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:38.120
WRGP?

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:39.530
Yeah.  Have some tea.

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:40.850
Thank you.

00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:46.320
We want to test ourselves 
and see how far we can go.

00:05:47.350 --> 00:05:50.290
So you're testing yourselves?  How 
did you do in the preliminaries?

00:05:50.770 --> 00:05:51.760
Yay!

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:55.430
You won!  That means you're 
also in the final tournament!

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:56.880
"Also?"

00:05:57.680 --> 00:05:59.400
That means…

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:02.520
I'm Rua.  I'm part of Team 5D's.

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:03.880
5D's?

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:07.010
That's Yusei Fudo's team!

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:09.980
Yeah, but I'm only in the pit crew.

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:11.990
So you're nothing special.

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:16.020
Wow, Rua!  You're on the same team as Yusei!

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:20.090
I'm a huge Yusei fan!  I 
like how he never gives up!

00:06:20.090 --> 00:06:21.420
Can I get his autograph?

00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:23.540
I can get it for you, but…

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:25.120
Really?

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:27.370
Wait a second!  I know I have my notebook...

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:30.730
Team 5D's.  That means you're our rival.

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:32.700
You're right.

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:34.710
We're Team Taiyo.

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:36.240
I'm Taro, the leader.

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:37.780
This is Jinbei and Yoshizo.

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:38.810
Nice to meet you.

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:39.720
Yeah.

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:44.780
But wait a second.  You're entering the 
final tournament using that D-Wheel?

00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:48.450
Of course.  That's our only D-Wheel.

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:50.090
Your only D-Wheel?

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:52.390
Yeah.  All three of us use it.

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:54.850
What?  The three of you 
share that piece of junk?

00:06:56.480 --> 00:06:57.770
I'm sorry.

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:01.030
It's fine.  There's no need to apologize.

00:07:01.030 --> 00:07:02.700
It is a piece of junk.

00:07:03.010 --> 00:07:05.940
But for us, it's a precious D-Wheel.

00:07:05.950 --> 00:07:10.060
The three of us worked together 
to build that D-Wheel.

00:07:10.870 --> 00:07:11.760
Taro…

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:14.270
But they attacked us.

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:15.510
"They?"

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:17.980
That gang during the preliminaries.

00:07:17.980 --> 00:07:19.180
That's Ghost!

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:20.120
Ghost?

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:22.450
Yeah.  That's what Yusei calls them.

00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:25.700
They destroyed our D-Wheel.

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:34.280
We're trying to repair it, 
but it's not going well.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:37.070
Then you should ask for Yusei's help.

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:38.440
Yusei?

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:40.440
Yeah.  Yusei will fix it.

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:42.910
He knows everything about D-Wheels.

00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:44.330
Want to go?

00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:46.440
Thanks for your offer, but…

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:51.250
We want to repair that D-Wheel ourselves.

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:58.160
Because we all gathered 
parts to build that D-Wheel.

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:02.090
But you're in trouble 
because you can't fix it.

00:08:02.090 --> 00:08:05.620
If you don't have a D-Wheel, you 
can't enter the final tournament.

00:08:07.570 --> 00:08:10.900
Let's ask Yusei.  He'll definitely fix it.

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:13.570
And you can enter the final tournament.

00:08:13.570 --> 00:08:15.430
Let's go ask.

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:17.530
We said that we don't need any help!

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:21.210
Everyone makes fun of us because 
they think we're country bumpkins!

00:08:21.210 --> 00:08:22.040
Jin!

00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:26.380
That's not what I meant.  
I just want to help.

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:28.600
And it's none of your business!

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:37.790
Fine.  Do whatever you want.

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:38.460
Rua!

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:39.390
Let him go!

00:08:46.840 --> 00:08:51.160
What's with that attitude?  
I just wanted to help.

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:03.000
There's not much time until 
the final tournament.

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:05.550
I know.  Let's look at the engine again.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.440
It's no good.

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:29.280
Repair a D-Wheel?

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:30.980
They're called Team Taiyo.

00:09:30.980 --> 00:09:34.900
Ghost destroyed their only D-Wheel.

00:09:35.030 --> 00:09:39.380
They told me to leave 
them alone, but I can't.

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:42.140
I understand.  I'll go.

00:09:42.360 --> 00:09:43.350
Really?

00:09:43.510 --> 00:09:45.360
A homemade D-Wheel?

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:47.970
That sounds interesting.  I'll go too!

00:09:47.970 --> 00:09:50.540
Thank you, Yusei and Bruno!

00:09:58.140 --> 00:09:59.840
It still won't start.

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:01.480
What are we going to do, Taro?

00:10:01.480 --> 00:10:04.230
We won't be able to enter 
the final tournament.

00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:05.130
Damn!

00:10:10.810 --> 00:10:11.660
Rua?

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:13.280
It's Yusei!

00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:19.520
I know it's none of my business, but 
just in case you didn't fix it yet…

00:10:19.730 --> 00:10:21.730
So this is the homemade D-Wheel!

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:22.190
Don't touch it!

00:10:23.590 --> 00:10:26.070
I said we don't need your help!

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:30.340
Thank you, Rua.  We're having trouble.

00:10:30.990 --> 00:10:31.710
Taro!

00:10:32.330 --> 00:10:35.950
I'm sorry, Jin, but I don't 
know what to do anymore.

00:10:35.950 --> 00:10:38.590
But that doesn't mean we need their help!

00:10:38.590 --> 00:10:40.670
We've done everything by ourselves!

00:10:40.670 --> 00:10:43.950
We didn't rely on others!  
It was just the three of us!

00:10:44.980 --> 00:10:45.790
Taro!

00:10:47.170 --> 00:10:51.170
Jin, are you fine if we can't 
enter the final tournament?

00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:55.130
In the beginning, I didn't 
know if we could win.

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:56.350
But we won.

00:10:56.350 --> 00:10:59.210
I thought it was luck, but 
we won the next match.

00:10:59.530 --> 00:11:01.350
Then we passed the preliminaries.

00:11:02.530 --> 00:11:07.810
Jin, you may be right that it's 
worth fighting solely by ourselves.

00:11:08.010 --> 00:11:10.220
But I want to enter.

00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:16.660
I want to enter the final tournament 
and see how our dueling stacks up!

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:18.400
Taro…

00:11:20.120 --> 00:11:21.180
Please, Jin.

00:11:21.180 --> 00:11:24.820
If we can't use this D-Wheel, we 
can't enter the final tournament.

00:11:27.350 --> 00:11:28.180
Jin…

00:11:31.770 --> 00:11:32.920
Do what you like!

00:11:34.470 --> 00:11:35.760
Thank you, Jin.

00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:37.710
Please help us.

00:11:38.020 --> 00:11:38.860
Yeah.

00:11:39.580 --> 00:11:41.670
He already started.

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:44.770
Wow!  What an interesting setup!

00:11:47.990 --> 00:11:49.080
Yusei.

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:50.990
Hey, Aki.

00:11:50.990 --> 00:11:53.520
Yusei is out with Bruno and Rua.

00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:55.080
I see…

00:11:57.450 --> 00:11:59.320
Exhibition duel?

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:04.700
In order to add excitement to the final 
tournament, Yeager asked Team Ragnarok for a favor.

00:12:05.180 --> 00:12:07.310
He would do something like that.

00:12:07.310 --> 00:12:09.090
Sounds fun.

00:12:09.090 --> 00:12:11.780
Team Ragnarok are duelists that use the three

00:12:11.780 --> 00:12:14.780
Aesir.  It's said that those cards have godlike powers.

00:12:14.780 --> 00:12:19.750
They'll definitely make it far in the 
tournament, so it's worth checking them out.

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:21.470
Want to go?

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:24.620
I guess.  I'll go with you.

00:12:43.790 --> 00:12:44.940
I see.

00:12:45.270 --> 00:12:48.150
This empty can transmits Moment energy.

00:12:48.150 --> 00:12:51.780
It's the best substitute when 
you don't have a regulator.

00:12:51.780 --> 00:12:52.790
Umm…

00:12:54.050 --> 00:12:55.760
Umm...  Well...

00:12:56.210 --> 00:12:58.060
Can I have your autograph?

00:12:58.060 --> 00:13:01.650
For my mom and dad and grandpa and 
grandma and my neighbor Tagosaku!

00:13:05.570 --> 00:13:07.310
They're all Normal Monsters.

00:13:07.650 --> 00:13:08.360
You fool!

00:13:08.670 --> 00:13:10.990
Never show anyone our deck!

00:13:11.370 --> 00:13:13.190
You're unbelievable!

00:13:13.190 --> 00:13:17.340
I forgot my notebook, so I had 
nothing else that he could sign.

00:13:17.340 --> 00:13:20.740
He might be our dueling 
opponent in the future!

00:13:21.040 --> 00:13:23.980
I'm sorry.  I'll be careful from now on.

00:13:26.090 --> 00:13:27.070
What's this?

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:30.720
A hanger?

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:32.990
Why is that in here?

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:37.920
I usually use it when I don't have a Y-hook.

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:41.460
It's flexible and fits easily.

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:42.870
I see.

00:13:43.280 --> 00:13:48.330
A long time ago, I also used to 
gather parts and build D-Wheels.

00:13:48.520 --> 00:13:49.940
You, Yusei?

00:13:49.940 --> 00:13:52.570
Yeah, when I was still in Satellite.

00:13:52.830 --> 00:13:56.690
I used everything, from 
scrap wood on cars to toys.

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:11.360
Here they come!

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:16.000
The favorites to win the 
WRGP final tournament!

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:18.400
The duelists who came from the land of god!

00:14:18.400 --> 00:14:22.350
Team Ragnarok!

00:14:39.620 --> 00:14:44.050
Team Ragnarok are the mightiest duelists in the world

00:14:44.050 --> 00:14:47.850
and use the three god-powered Aesir - Odin, Thor and Loki.

00:14:48.020 --> 00:14:53.480
There are many legends about this 
professional Riding Duel team!

00:14:56.710 --> 00:14:58.530
So that's Team Ragnarok.

00:14:58.530 --> 00:15:00.140
They have incredible presence.

00:15:00.140 --> 00:15:02.400
It's like they're really 
from the land of god.

00:15:02.770 --> 00:15:06.320
The power of god?  They're bluffing.

00:15:08.540 --> 00:15:10.920
Let's begin the exhibition duel!

00:15:10.920 --> 00:15:16.020
Dragan, the man who has the skills on 
an angry god, will choose the opponent!

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:28.520
You're my opponent!

00:15:29.020 --> 00:15:31.010
Jack Atlas!

00:15:31.220 --> 00:15:35.500
Whoa!  Dragan chose the 
former King Jack Atlas!

00:15:36.190 --> 00:15:40.310
God versus King!  This is 
going to be an exciting duel!

00:15:40.970 --> 00:15:43.450
Fine!  I'll be your opponent!

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:53.570
Bring it!  I'll make you regret choosing me!

00:15:57.790 --> 00:16:00.130
What's up with Dragan?

00:16:00.130 --> 00:16:02.360
I'm sensing strange powers.

00:16:08.330 --> 00:16:09.520
Duel!

00:16:10.810 --> 00:16:14.040
I'll go first!  My turn!

00:16:14.310 --> 00:16:17.120
I summon Tanngrisnir of the Nordic Beasts!

00:16:17.930 --> 00:16:20.620
I set one card and end my turn!

00:16:20.710 --> 00:16:22.620
1200 attack points?

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:26.120
You can't defeat Jack Atlas 
with a card like that!

00:16:26.120 --> 00:16:27.320
My turn!

00:16:27.770 --> 00:16:30.160
I Special Summon Vice Dragon.

00:16:31.560 --> 00:16:37.460
I can Special Summon this card from my 
hand when monsters are only on your field.

00:16:37.460 --> 00:16:41.170
If I Special Summon it using this 
effect, its attack points are halved.

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:44.440
Then I summon Dark Resonator!

00:16:44.650 --> 00:16:49.110
Level 3 Dark Resonator 
tunes Level 5 Vice Dragon.

00:16:49.830 --> 00:16:52.530
The pulse of the King now forms a line here!

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:54.890
Witness the power of the rumbling heavens!

00:16:55.080 --> 00:16:56.320
Synchro Summon!

00:16:56.780 --> 00:17:00.220
My soul!  Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:17:01.030 --> 00:17:06.020
Jack Atlas's ace monster Red Dragon 
Archfiend has already appeared!

00:17:09.520 --> 00:17:11.440
Red Dragon Archfiend...

00:17:11.610 --> 00:17:15.040
Red Dragon Archfiend attacks 
Tanngrisnir of the Nordic Beasts!

00:17:15.320 --> 00:17:18.010
Absolute Powerforce!

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:24.720
Dragan instantly took 1800 points of damage!

00:17:27.630 --> 00:17:32.070
I didn't know the former King's 
attack would be so weak.

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:32.900
What?

00:17:32.900 --> 00:17:38.630
When Tanngrisnir of the Nordic Beasts is 
destroyed, I can Special Summon two Nordic Beast Tokens.

00:17:40.470 --> 00:17:43.050
I set one card and end my turn.

00:17:43.510 --> 00:17:44.690
My turn!

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:47.820
I Special Summon Guldfaxe 
of the Nordic Beasts!

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:55.050
When a Synchro Monster is on your field, I 
can Special Summon this card from my hand.

00:17:55.350 --> 00:18:00.730
Level 4 Guldfaxe of the Nordic Beasts 
tunes two Level 3 Nordic Beast Tokens.

00:18:01.450 --> 00:18:06.780
When the gate to the star world opens, the 
ancient god of battle swings its magical hammer.

00:18:06.780 --> 00:18:10.090
As the earth trembles, it 
arrives with roaring thunder!

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:12.100
Synchro Summon!

00:18:13.730 --> 00:18:14.510
It's coming!

00:18:26.720 --> 00:18:29.210
Come, Thor, Lord of the Aesir!

00:18:32.450 --> 00:18:35.390
Dragan's ace has appeared!

00:18:35.390 --> 00:18:38.420
The god card Thor, Lord of the Aesir!

00:18:38.790 --> 00:18:39.930
That's...

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:42.300
One of the three Aesir.

00:18:46.610 --> 00:18:47.750
What?

00:18:49.000 --> 00:18:51.270
What's happening?

00:18:56.360 --> 00:19:00.160
Crimson Dragon and the god's 
powers are resonating!

00:19:02.610 --> 00:19:06.240
Thor, Lord of the Aesir 
attacks Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:07.840
Thunder Pile!

00:19:08.030 --> 00:19:09.800
Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:19:29.690 --> 00:19:31.440
They're resonating.

